@startuml Séquence 2 - Prédiction automatique météo

actor "Utilisateur" as User
participant "Frontend\n(Vue.js)" as Frontend
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Forecast\nService" as ForecastSvc
participant "Open-Meteo\nAPI" as OpenMeteo
participant "GeoData\nService" as GeoDatasvc
participant "Forecast\nEngine" as Engine
participant "Random Forest\nModel" as RFModel
participant "Scaler" as Scaler

title Scénario: Prédiction automatique des inondations pour une zone

== Sélection de la zone ==
User -> Frontend: Sélectionne zone\n"Dakar Keur Massar"
Frontend -> Frontend: Récupère coordonnées\nlat=15.43058, lon=-15.887329

== Requête de prédiction ==
Frontend -> Gateway: POST /predict_meteo_auto\n{zone: "dakar_keur_massar"}
Gateway -> ForecastSvc: Forward request

== Récupération données météo ==
ForecastSvc -> OpenMeteo: GET forecast?\nlat=15.43058&lon=-15.887329\n&hourly=temp,humidity,precip\n&forecast_days=5

alt Données météo disponibles
    OpenMeteo --> ForecastSvc: JSON hourly data\n(5 jours × 24h)
else API météo indisponible
    OpenMeteo --> ForecastSvc: Error 502
    ForecastSvc --> Gateway: {error: "Service météo indisponible"}
    Gateway --> Frontend: Error response
    Frontend --> User: ❌ Service temporairement indisponible
end

== Calcul contexte géographique ==
opt Région avec données géospatiales
    ForecastSvc -> GeoDatasvc: compute_context_features(\nlat, lon, region="dakar")
    GeoDatasvc -> GeoDatasvc: load_layer("dakar",\n"Axe_ecoulement_temporaire")
    GeoDatasvc -> GeoDatasvc: calculate distance_to_flow
    GeoDatasvc -> GeoDatasvc: load_layer("dakar",\n"Zone_inondable_humide")
    GeoDatasvc -> GeoDatasvc: check if point inside
    GeoDatasvc --> ForecastSvc: {distance_to_flow_m: 320,\ninside_flood_zone: false}
end

== Agrégation et prédiction jour par jour ==
loop Pour chaque jour (J à J+5)
    ForecastSvc -> Engine: aggregate_daily_features(\nday_slice, recent_precip)
    Engine -> Engine: Calcule:\n- precip_sum (1j)\n- precip_3d_sum\n- precip_7d_sum\n- precip_15d_sum\n- humidity_mean/max\n- temp_mean/max
    Engine --> ForecastSvc: feature_vector[9 features]

    ForecastSvc -> Engine: predict_from_features(\nvector, rf_model, scaler)
    Engine -> Engine: _as_model_input(features)
    Engine -> Scaler: transform(features)
    Scaler --> Engine: scaled_features
    Engine -> RFModel: predict_proba(scaled_features)
    RFModel --> Engine: [proba_no_flood, proba_flood]
    Engine -> Engine: prediction = \n(proba_flood >= 0.35) ? 1 : 0
    Engine --> ForecastSvc: PredictionResult(\nprediction=1,\nproba_inondation=0.72)

    ForecastSvc -> ForecastSvc: results.append({\n  date, precip_sums,\n  proba, inondation,\n  geo_context\n})
end

== Retour des résultats ==
ForecastSvc --> Gateway: {\n  zone: "dakar_keur_massar",\n  geo_context: {...},\n  results: [5 prédictions]\n}
Gateway --> Frontend: Predictions JSON
Frontend -> Frontend: Affiche graphique\nChart.js (courbes)
Frontend --> User: 📊 Prédictions 5 jours:\n✓ J+1: 72% risque\n✓ J+2: 45% risque\n✓ J+3: 23% risque\n...

note right of Engine
  Features extraites:
  1. precipitation_mm_sum
  2. precipitation_mm_max
  3. relative_humidity_2m_pct_mean
  4. relative_humidity_2m_pct_max
  5. temperature_2m_degc_mean
  6. temperature_2m_degc_max
  7. precip_3d_sum (rolling)
  8. precip_7d_sum (rolling)
  9. precip_15d_sum (rolling)
end note

note right of RFModel
  Seuil de décision: 0.35
  Si proba >= 0.35 → Inondation
  Sinon → Pas d'inondation
end note

@enduml
